course: dictionary
lesson: 1187
title: One word, several meanings: bruise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. Bruise can be a noun (a thing: a bruise) or a verb (an action: to bruise). «At home Jake's little brother Alfie took one look at the new bruise on Jake's cheek and burst into tears.» Here a bruise is a mark on the skin.
explain: Look for clues in the words around it. «Grief usually gets softer with time» is about feelings, so when Oscar's grandad says «like a bruise that's healing», he means a feeling that is still sore when touched but no longer sharp all the time.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In «a bruise gets something cold», the bruise is the thing that needs care, so it must be a mark on the body, not a spot on fruit. A bruise forms when tiny blood vessels under the skin break, but the skin itself is not broken.
fact: A bruise is a purple, blue or dark mark on the skin, caused by a bump or knock.
fact: A bruise happens when tiny blood vessels under the skin break, but the skin is not broken.
fact: «Bruise» can also mean a soft, brown, damaged spot on fruit, like a bruise on an apple.
fact: As a verb, «bruise» means to get or give a bruise, as in «I bruised my arm.»
fact: A cold pack wrapped in a cloth helps reduce swelling and pain.
exercise: «Small injuries need simple, correct care: a cut is cleaned and covered, a bruise gets something cold, and a burn goes under cool running water for 20 minutes.» What does a bruise need, according to this sentence? | Stitches | Cool running water for 20 minutes | A hot drink | *Something cold
exercise: Mia says, «I bruised my arm when I fell off my bike.» Which word is the verb? | arm | *bruised | bike | fell
exercise: «Oscar's grandad says that a year after his wife died the pain is like a bruise that's healing.» What does this comparison suggest? | A piece of fruit that has gone bad | A feeling of being hungry | A feeling that has gone completely | *A feeling that is sore but getting better
test: In «the new bruise on Jake's cheek», what does bruise mean? | A cold pack | *A purple or blue mark on the skin | To hit someone hard | A soft brown spot on fruit
test: In «I bruised my arm», what does bruised mean? | A cold pack | A bruised apple | Very old | *To get a bruise on my arm
exam: Which care goes with a bruise, according to «a bruise gets something cold»? | Stitches and a plaster | *Something cold, such as a cold pack wrapped in a cloth | Sunlight | Running water for 20 minutes
